No line break right after opening punctuation (UAX #14 LB14): `(`, `[`, `{`, `“` and `«` keep to the word after them,
as upstream already keeps closing punctuation to the word before it (LB13). Without it a line could end between the two
brackets of `[[account]]`. Both wrapping paths take it: `LineWrapper::wrap_line` and the shaped line's
`LineLayout::compute_wrap_boundaries`, which every wrapped text element draws with. An upstream candidate (Zed).

--- a/src/text_system/line_layout.rs
